# CloudDrives uses an ALLOWLIST: everything is ignored unless it is explicitly listed below.
# This guards against accidentally committing secrets, tokens, logs or caches.
# Runtime data (tokens, settings, cache, logs) lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\CloudDrives - never in this folder.

/*
!/.github/
!/docs/
!/src/
!/tests/
!/tools/
!/.editorconfig
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore
!/.gitleaks.toml
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CloudDrives.bat
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.en.md
!/install.ps1
!/LICENSE
!/PRIVACY.md
!/PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

# Never commit these - not even inside allowed folders.
*.conf
*.conf.*
*.log
*.log.*
*.dpapi
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.token
*.secret
*.zip
*.msi
*.exe
*.dll
settings.json
settings.json.*
recovery-kit*
CloudDrives-Recovery*
client_secret*.json
TestResults/
testResults*.xml
coverage*.xml
